===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To stay in a flophouse.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1941|title=The Court of Missing Heirs |author=James F. Waters  |page=53 |ISBN=|passage=August was aware of Robert's strange quirk of '''flophousing''' away from home and that he often spent weekends at the Diana. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1960|title=All the naked heroes: a novel |author=Alan Kapelner  |page=337 |ISBN=|passage=I kept going nowhere, bummed the country, boxcar'd it, breadlined it, '''flophoused''' it, that cruddy dying by inches in jungles when, Christ-o, outa the knocked-out black and blue I'm told I gotta go to war, gotta fight for freedom. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1989 |title=Fine Arts |author=S. Prideaux  |page=202 |ISBN=|passage=For old time's sake we plan to '''flophouse''' with you over the parturient period. }}

